INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Benchmark web research: Ronin Bridge and Harmony Horizon thefts", "source_url": "SRC-001; SRC-002; SRC-003; SRC-004", "text": "Findings from benchmark sources. SRC-003 (Elliptic, Mar 29 2022): Ronin Network announced theft of 173,600 ETH and 25.5m USDC, worth $540m at theft; OFAC on Apr 14 2022 sanctioned the thief's Ethereum address and listed its owner as Lazarus Group, a North Korean state hacking group. Ronin postmortem said attacker obtained five of nine validator private keys and evidence pointed to social engineering. Elliptic said stolen USDC was swapped to ETH via DEXs to avoid issuer seizure and centralized-exchange AML/KYC; $16.7m ETH was sent through three centralized exchanges, then strategy shifted to Tornado Cash after exchanges said they would cooperate; $80.3m ETH had gone through Tornado Cash, $9.7m was in intermediary wallets, and $433m remained in original wallet as of Apr 14. Elliptic assessed similarities with prior Lazarus attacks in victim location, suspected social engineering, and laundering pattern.\nSRC-002 (Chainalysis, Sep 8 2022): Ronin theft was over $600m at time of report; Lazarus Group gained five of nine validator keys and approved withdrawals of 173,600 ETH and 25.5m USDC. Laundering used over 12,000 addresses. Chainalysis described a typical North Korea DeFi laundering sequence: intermediary wallets; ETH mixed in Tornado Cash; swap to BTC; BTC mixed; deposit to crypto-to-fiat services. Ronin funds also used cross-chain hopping: ETH to BNB, swap to USDD, bridge to BitTorrent. More than $30m was seized, approximately 10% of stolen funds, and much remained in wallets.\nSRC-001 (Elliptic, May 9 2023): FBI confirmed North Korea-backed Lazarus Group behind June 2022 Harmony Horizon Bridge hack. Horizon was exploited for $99.7m. Elliptic said attribution followed similarities to Lazarus blockchain laundering patterns. It reported programmatic structuring through Tornado Cash, mirroring Ronin laundering; more than $555m from the two hacks reportedly went through Tornado Cash, including >$468m Ronin and $96m Harmony. After Tornado Cash sanctions, Harmony funds were structured into Railgun deposits beginning Jan 2023; Elliptic estimated around 70% of Railgun volume was Harmony funds, reducing mixer effectiveness. On-chain data reportedly showed deposits into three exchanges; Binance and Huobi said they identified, blocked, and seized some funds. SRC-004 provides no substantive hack text. No benchmark source establishes that APT38 is an alias for Lazarus Group, and no specific wallet addresses were returned beyond the description of the sanctioned Ronin exploiter Ethereum address."}
